  universityChannels: 'UK universities admit via UCAS (Universities and Colleges Admissions Service). Cambridge A-Level is the primary UK qualification for undergraduate entry, with IB Diploma equally accepted and American AP case-dependent (typically requires SAT/ACT + AP portfolio). Oxbridge (Oxford + Cambridge) apply via UCAS with October 15 early deadline and additional admissions tests (many now standardised via UAT-UK for humanities and various subject-specific tests). Personalised university guidance sessions with the Head of Academics including UCAS personal statement coaching and Oxbridge / Russell Group interview preparation for elite candidates.',
  cambridgeCardDescription: 'Smartious\'s primary offer for UK families. Cambridge IGCSE (Years 10-11) and Cambridge A-Level (Years 12-13) delivered as live online classes with morning UK delivery matching Nairobi lunchtime teaching. Private candidate examination registration at UK Cambridge Assessment International Education authorised centres (hundreds of venues nationwide). Pathway accepted by all UK universities via UCAS including Oxbridge (Oxford + Cambridge) for elite candidates, plus US Ivy League via Common Application, Canadian U15, Australian Group of Eight.',
  britishCurriculumSuits: 'UK families across all situations targeting Cambridge IGCSE + A-Level pathway. Best fit for: (1) Elective Home Education families under Section 7 Education Act 1996 needing accredited curriculum provider, (2) Section 19 alternative provision students (excluded, school refuser, medically-unable), (3) SEND students where mainstream physical school has not worked, (4) fee-sensitive independent-school-track families (Smartious ~£1,700-£5,100/year vs London independent £26,000-£52,000+/year), (5) fee-sensitive online school families (below Cambridge Home School Online £10,950/year), (6) UK families temporarily abroad (Forces personnel, contractors, expat rotations), (7) Private candidate 16-18+ retake candidates, (8) Gifted students needing acceleration beyond year group.',
  britishCurriculumDelivery: 'Live online classes GMT 10 AM – 1 PM (BST 11 AM – 2 PM), small groups 4-6 students. Cambridge examinations at UK Cambridge-authorised centres.',
  ibDiplomaSuits: 'UK families targeting IB Diploma\'s breadth rather than Cambridge A-Level narrow specialism. Best fit for: (1) families targeting US Ivy League preferring holistic pathway, (2) families targeting universities that specifically value IB Diploma\'s breadth alongside Cambridge subject depth, (3) internationally mobile UK families expecting overseas moves during Sixth Form.',
  ibDiplomaDelivery: 'Live online IB DP classes across all six subject groups plus Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay supervision.',
  americanCurriculumSuits: 'UK families targeting US universities via Common Application. AP portfolio strengthens US applications; SAT/ACT preparation integrated. Best fit for: (1) families with strong US university preference, (2) UK families with US relocations planned, (3) UK families targeting specifically US-focused university destinations (Ivy League, Stanford, UC system, MIT, Caltech).',
  americanCurriculumDelivery: 'American Curriculum with AP courses Grades 9-12, SAT/ACT preparation, Common App essay coaching.',
  founderBioCountrySpecific: 'Alfred Ouko founded Smartious in 2019 to make international qualifications (Cambridge, IB, American, Ontario OSSD) accessible to families across emerging markets, Elective Home Education families, and international corporate rotational communities at online-delivery fees below traditional independent school and existing UK online school competitor pricing. UK families join students in 19 other countries — from London Kensington to Dubai Downtown, Manchester Salford to Kuala Lumpur Mont Kiara, Edinburgh New Town to Tokyo Ebisu.',
  founderUniversitySpecialism: 'Alfred holds a BEd in Mathematics and Physics — Smartious\'s Cambridge A-Level and IB Diploma STEM subjects are led personally when needed. Head of Academics supervises curriculum delivery and university placement strategy per family including UCAS personal statement coaching and Oxbridge / Russell Group interview preparation.',

  competitorsIntro: 'UK online school competition is genuinely mature — Cambridge Home School Online (CHS Online) leads at £10,950/year secondary / £6,099/year prep with live classes ≤10 pupils and UK ISI accreditation. King\'s InterHigh (£8,000-15,000/year), My Online Schooling (£10,000+/year), InterHigh, Immanuel Online School operate the mid-tier. Wolsey Hall Oxford is the self-paced budget alternative at £4,000-£7,000/year (no live classes). Smartious sits BELOW this competitive set at USD 2,160-6,480/year (~£1,700-£5,100/year) with LIVE small-group classes (4-6 pupils tighter than CHS\'s 10) and cross-country cohort. UK independent schools operate at fundamentally different fee tier — London premium day £26,000-£30,000+/year, London boarding (Eton, Harrow) £48,000-£52,000+/year, Manchester/Birmingham/Leeds/Bristol premium day £15,000-£30,000+/year — the traditional fee-arbitrage market where Smartious offers dramatic savings with identical Cambridge / IB / American qualifications and UCAS pathway.',
