  faqs: [
    { q: 'How does Smartious compare to Cambridge Home School Online (CHS Online) — the UK online school market leader?',                          a: 'CHS Online (£10,950/year secondary, £6,099/year prep, live classes ≤10 pupils, Cambridge UK-based, ISI accredited, Oxbridge/Russell Group prep) is the UK\'s most-established online selective independent school. Smartious sits BELOW at USD 2,160-6,480/year (~£1,700-£5,100/year) with LIVE small-group classes 4-6 pupils (tighter than CHS\'s ≤10) and cross-country cohort providing global peer network. Smartious does NOT hold UK ISI accreditation — for families specifically valuing UK-specific ISI status, CHS is the appropriate choice. Smartious qualifications (Cambridge IGCSE, A-Level, IB, AP, OSSD) are awarded by international examination boards regardless of school accreditation status and provide the same UCAS pathway.' },
    { q: 'How does Smartious compare to UK independent schools like Westminster, Eton, or Harrow?',                                                a: 'UK independent schools — Westminster (£30,000+/year day, London), Eton College (£52,000+/year boarding), Harrow (£48,000+/year boarding), St. Paul\'s (£30,000+/year), Manchester Grammar School (£30,000+/year) — provide physical campus premium British education with boarding, sport, arts, pastoral, and university preparation infrastructure. Smartious provides live online Cambridge / IB / American / OSSD at USD 2,160-6,480/year (~£1,700-£5,100/year) with identical qualifications, UCAS pathway including Oxbridge for elite candidates, and cross-country cohort. Fee arbitrage substantial; qualifications and university pathway identical.' },
    { q: 'We\'re Elective Home Education (EHE) family in England. Does Smartious meet the "suitable education" standard?',                          a: 'Yes. England Section 7 Education Act 1996 makes parents responsible for "suitable education" — no specific curriculum required. Smartious as accredited international curriculum provider delivering Cambridge IGCSE, A-Level, IB Diploma, American AP, or Ontario OSSD meets this standard. Documented curriculum, contact hours, assessments, and progress reporting suitable for local authority enquiry response.' },
    { q: 'Our child cannot attend mainstream school (medical, behavioural, exclusion, refuser). Can our local authority commission Smartious under Section 19?',   a: 'Local authorities have STATUTORY duty under Section 19 Education Act 1996 to arrange education for children unable to attend mainstream school. Smartious can serve these students directly (family funds) or potentially via local authority Alternative Provision commissioning arrangements (LA funds). We can support Section 19 conversations with your local authority.' },
    { q: 'Where do UK students sit Cambridge IGCSE and A-Level examinations?',                                                                     a: 'Cambridge Assessment International Education has hundreds of authorised examination centres across the UK — private schools accepting external candidates, FE colleges, British Council venues (British Council London for example). Smartious handles examination registration logistics. Exam fees are separate from Smartious tuition and paid directly to examination centre (typically £80-£150 per subject entry).' },
    { q: 'What UK universities accept Cambridge IGCSE, A-Level, IB, and AP qualifications?',                                                       a: 'All UK universities via UCAS accept Cambridge A-Level and IB Diploma (American AP case-dependent, typically requires SAT/ACT + AP portfolio). Oxford, Cambridge, Imperial College London, LSE, UCL, King\'s College London, Warwick, Bristol, Manchester, Edinburgh, Durham, Bath, Exeter, York, Southampton, Nottingham, Sheffield, Birmingham, Leeds, Newcastle, Cardiff, Belfast (rest of Russell Group).' },
    { q: 'Our child has SEND (Special Educational Needs and Disabilities). Can Smartious accommodate?',                                            a: 'Smartious live small-group classes (4-6 students, tighter than CHS Online\'s ≤10) provide small-group learning environment many neurodivergent students need but mainstream schools cannot deliver at scale. Structured routine, low sensory load compared to physical classroom, camera-optional participation. However, we are not a specialist SEND provider — for students with EHCPs (Education, Health and Care Plans) or high-support-need SEND, please contact us to discuss specific needs.' },
    { q: 'We\'re Scottish family. Scotland uses CfE with Highers, not GCSE/A-Level. Why choose Cambridge via Smartious?',                          a: 'Scottish universities admit primarily via UCAS with Highers / Advanced Highers, but Cambridge A-Level is directly UCAS-accepted for Scottish universities. Cambridge A-Level is essential for UK-outside-Scotland universities (Oxford, Cambridge, Imperial, LSE, UCL, Russell Group) and directly recognised globally. Smartious serves Scottish families specifically preferring Cambridge / A-Level pathway.' },
    { q: 'We\'re UK Forces or expat family temporarily abroad. How does Smartious support continuity?',                                            a: 'UK Forces personnel, international contractors, diplomatic British Embassy families, and general expat rotations continue Cambridge / A-Level trajectory seamlessly through overseas postings. Return to UK maintains curriculum continuity for reintegration to UK schools or university pathway.' },
    { q: 'What internet speed does Smartious require in the UK?',                                                                                  a: 'Sustained ~5-10 Mbps per student for live HD video conferencing. BT Fibre, Virgin Media, Sky Broadband, and Vodafone UK 5G residential broadband across UK cities routinely deliver 100+ Mbps. Rural UK areas with adequate ~10-50 Mbps broadband also supported.' },
  ],

